WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
Two metal plates, with
only air between them.

2
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.800
Connect a cell.

3
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.950
Electrons leave one plate,
travel around the circuit,

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.350
and land on the other.

5
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.150
None crosses the gap.

6
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.460
Charge a 470 microfarad
capacitor to 9 volts,

7
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.400
and about 26 million
billion electrons move.

8
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:23.130
One plate ends at plus
Q, the other at minus Q:

9
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.050
net charge zero.

10
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.510
So what is it actually storing?

11
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.010
In this mission, you'll
define capacitance,

12
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:36.060
and meet the farad: a unit so huge that
real capacitors use millionths of one.

13
00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.900
Then you'll double the
voltage on the same capacitor,

14
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.630
and see what changes and what stays fixed.

15
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.030
Your mission: find out what a
charged capacitor is really storing.
